# Git on Windows normalises line endings, which silently CORRUPTS binary files.
# The reference manual is a PDF: without this it would be checked out with CRLF
# substitutions and stop opening. The sizes happen to match today because the
# file has no bare LF bytes in the wrong place -- that is luck, not a guarantee.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.exe binary

# Shell scripts must stay LF: bash refuses a script whose lines end in CR.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Model files must stay LF for a harder reason. The round-trip guarantee is
# BYTE-identical, and the reader drops CR while the writer emits LF -- so a
# file checked out with CRLF would come back different the moment a front end
# saved it, and the property this format is built on would be false on Windows.
*.des text eol=lf
